    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 241\n\nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nAssembly Bill Number 8562-A, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the executive law, in relation to state disaster\n      preparedness plans\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would require an amendment to the State  disaster  prepared-\nness plan to ensure delivery of medical supplies and medication to phar-\nmacies, hospitals and nursing homes during a disaster emergency.\n\n  I  agree  that  public-private  sector  coordination  is  an essential\nelement of any comprehensive emergency management  plan,  which  is  why\nexisting  law authorizes private entities to participate in the planning\nprocess.\n\n  First, emergency management statutes must give local chief  executives\ndiscretion  to  address  the  unique  needs of their jurisdictions. This\nincludes the flexibility to exercise the appropriate discretion based on\nevent-specific factors. Arbitrarily narrowing the  scope  and  focus  of\nemergency planning and response efforts by singling out a specific group\nor type of provider is not sound emergency management practice.\n\n  Second,  travel  restrictions  and  road  closures cannot be made in a\nvacuum or without appropriate knowledge. Rather, they must be made  only\nafter  evaluating  the  specific  circumstances  of the disaster and the\navailability of resources. As this bill does not  align  with  emergency\nmanagement best practices, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 241,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2016
   }
  ],
  "size": 1
 },
